WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.700
Dr. Eggman, you're working too fast!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.120
I'm not broken!

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.120
Don't take me apart!

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.250
Why are you so hyper?

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.300
Take it easy.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.420
Don't you understand?

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:00.760
I'm going to get my revenge on Sonic by using this.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.640
Whoa! That's...

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.020
Just watch, Sonic!

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.480
Sorry to keep you waiting, Dr. Eggman!

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.490
We should've escaped like this from the beginning.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:25.620
Shut up! Timing is important.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.580
You just wait, Sonic!

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.580
You'll witness the hell of electrical appliance robots!

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:44.100
Sonic, what's happened to this city?

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.980
Sonic, how do you like fighting against electrical appliance robots?

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.190
This will be the last time that I'll see you.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.900
You'll be buried under a mountain of electrical appliances and die!

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.660
Knuckles, you better not run out of energy.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.700
That's my line!

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.190
We're finally done.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:34.980
Yeah.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.230
How?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:38.690
How can they use water?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.740
Someone must have fixed it.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.410
They should mind their own business.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:47.200
Damn. We were so close to succeeding.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.290
So what! Let's defeat Sonic by ourselves!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.620
Did you hear what he said?

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:53.620
What do you want to do, Dr. Eggman?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.790
Okay then!

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.000
Retreat.

00:03:56.790 --> 00:04:00.340
Wait, Dr. Eggman! Don't leave me alone!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.410
Episode 44

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.410
The Ridiculous Epic Spy Battle

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.540
Eggman escaped from prison.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:36.080
What evil act should I do to throw the world into chaos?

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.960
He must be captured, no matter what.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:45.130
Is this why you called us?

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.720
Topaz!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.470
This is what the secret mission is about?

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.430
Miss Rouge!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.190
So all we have to do is find Eggman's whereabouts.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.440
The Intelligence Agency is also looking for him, but...

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.450
Where's Eggman hiding?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:14.250
You know more about Eggman than the spies at Intelligence.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.620
What will be our reward?

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.960
You'll have as many sparkling objects as you like.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.460
Sparkling objects? What beautiful words!

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:25.010
It makes me swoon.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.880
Sheesh.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.930
I pray for your success!

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.150
Where do you think Eggman went?

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:48.160
I don't know, but he's definitely planning something evil.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.490
Did Sonic say anything about Eggman?

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:52.580
He did.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:53.660
What did he say?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.040
When I asked him, "Where do you think Eggman is?"

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.460
I don't care.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.630
That's just like him.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.470
You can say that again.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.430
Chris!

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:14.890
Cream, Cheese and Emerl.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:20.940
We were taking a stroll until we ended up at Chris's school.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:25.230
Emerl can quickly copy the abilities of another person.

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.650
Wow.

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.860
It's Mr. Stewart.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.410
This tree looks suspicious.

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.130
Eggman may be hiding inside this tree.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:59.940
That tickles!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:02.440
Just as I thought!

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.110
He found us!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.020
Let's get out of here!

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.230
Wait!

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.780
Mr. Stewart!

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:09.570
Oh no!

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:12.490
Mr. Stewart?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.290
What are you doing here?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:17.750
Bird watching.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:19.200
I also want to look!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.210
I can see!

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.710
I'm next.

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:35.800
Eggman?

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:36.930
What?

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.890
Eggman is buying a used book.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:40.140
Really?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.060
Give it back.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.440
It's really him.

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:47.440
Let's all catch Eggman together!

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:48.570
Yeah!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.070
No!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.320
Capturing Eggman is too dangerous.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.530
I'll tell the police about Eggman.

00:07:55.530 --> 00:08:00.870
So hurry on home and leave the rest to the police. Got it?

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.250
Got it?

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.330
I think that's a good idea too.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.050
Fine.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.220
Bye.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:15.340
Chris, wait up!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.520
I'll follow Eggman and find his hideout.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.770
Hey, taxi!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:36.450
What are you doing?

00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:38.330
I thought you all went home!

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.990
Forget about that.

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:43.120
Drive, Mr. Stewart!

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:45.960
Sheesh.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.220
Sonic!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.520
Sonic!

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:06.270
Chris hasn't come home from school yet.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:10.270
Cream, Cheese and Emerl also haven't returned from their stroll.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.070
I'm counting on you.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.290
Eggman's taxi has stopped!

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.800
He got off.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.020
Where did Eggman go?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.350
Did he find out that we were following him?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.660
Mr. Stewart?

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:17.130
Eggman is underground!

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:19.760
Where?

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.760
Let's find him!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:21.180
Over there!

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.070
Water!

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.990
Wow!

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.790
What's the matter, Danny?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:53.540
A lizard jumped in!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.800
Where?

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.010
Right there.

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:08.060
Danny, you're a man, so you can't be scared of lizards.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:10.520
Aren't you afraid, Helen?

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.610
No, because I've caught one before.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.110
Liar.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.820
Helen can even catch caterpillars.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:18.940
What?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:23.820
You're a little weird.

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.280
I'm not weird!

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:29.080
Stop it! This isn't the time to fight.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:30.540
They're laughing at you.

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.860
Playtime's over.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.230
Push.

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:31.140
Isn't it delicious?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.350
I guess.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.980
The President seemed troubled.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.110
He worries too much.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:41.030
When the time's right, we'll find Eggman's hideout.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.030
You think?

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.160
The wind has picked up recently.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.370
Can it be Sonic?

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.200
I wonder what he's doing?

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.370
I'll ask him the next time he runs by.

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.080
Sonic.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.880
You seem busy. What are you doing?

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.170
I'm looking for someone.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:00.250
Who?

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.090
Chris, Cream, Cheese and Emerl.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:06.010
If you happen to find Eggman along the way, let me know.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:13.100
Anyway, this is delicious.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.770
Isn't it?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.280
Eggman.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:30.280
What are you planning to do by buying those used books?

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:33.540
I'm using them for my next plan.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.370
What's your next plan?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:37.120
This world will-

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:41.420
Oops, I don't need tell you.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.260
Dr. Eggman.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.970
What is it, Decoe and Bocoe?

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:45.880
Well...

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.680
These objects were in the briefcase.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.260
It's his briefcase.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:55.140
Are you a government spy?

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:56.390
No!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:58.850
You're panicking. That's suspicious.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.610
Mr. Stewart is a spy?

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:02.770
Don't make me laugh.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:06.950
Yeah. Spies are much cooler.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.710
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.460
A guy like him could never be a spy.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:25.340
Well then, I'm going to concentrate on my experiments for my next plan.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.920
Farewell.

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:32.220
Why do you look so relieved?

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:34.810
It's as if you really are a spy.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.350
I'm a teacher.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:39.190
To put it more accurately, he's our former teacher.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.850
That's right.

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:46.070
What's Eggman's next plan?

00:14:46.070 --> 00:14:48.990
Why would we know?

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:52.200
He just makes us work really hard!

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.450
Bocoe.

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.750
Decoe.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:15:00.170
Let's go over there and cry.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.790
He must really work them hard.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.470
Let's think of a way to escape.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.130
Helen, I'm going to borrow this.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.480
Let's hurry up and go.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:42.540
Maybe Mr. Stewart really is a spy.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.170
I doubt it.

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.630
It's a dead end.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:53.840
No...

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:02.020
Let's do a science experiment.

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:06.230
If you mix substance A and substance B together...

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.490
Stand back!

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:18.410
It opened!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.810
This gate will open if you enter the password.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:45.520
Okay!

00:16:48.060 --> 00:16:49.110
Eggman?

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:52.190
Did you unlock the password?

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.320
No, this is too easy.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:56.910
This is probably a trap.

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.200
A trap?

00:16:58.370 --> 00:16:59.660
What will happen is...

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.630
I can't put these children in danger.

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:12.760
Let's think of another way to open it.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.260
Mr. Stewart!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.010
Let's think too!

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.810
If only we could communicate with Sonic...

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.440
Cream, look at that.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:40.580
It's that mischievous kid.

00:17:41.660 --> 00:17:44.290
Helen, I have an idea.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.620
Okay.

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:53.000
Ella's apple pie is the best!

00:17:56.680 --> 00:18:00.430
Ella is a genius when it comes to making apple pies!

00:18:00.430 --> 00:18:02.060
Apple pie?

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:07.440
I want to eat it!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:10.520
If you want to eat it, you have to go to Chris's house.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.400
If you tell her that you heard it from me, she'll give you some.

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:15.780
I'll tell her!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.320
Apple pie!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:26.080
If he gets in contact with Ella, then Sonic will definitely come.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.830
I hope it works out.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.120
I'm sure it will!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.050
Apple pie.

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.930
Chris's house is...

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.350
Hey, you.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.270
Where are you going?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:53.230
I'm going to see Ella at Chris's house so that I can eat apple pie.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.320
What?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.530
That means Chris is down here.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.650
Oh yeah. Hey.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.200
Will you pass a message to Topaz and Rouge for me?

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.370
No.

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:06.830
Ella's strawberry cake is great too.

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.040
Strawberry cake?

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:14.540
Will she make me some?

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.010
Of course.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.600
Vanilla is good, but chocolate is the best.

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.310
I like both.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:28.980
I have a message for you from Sonic.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:30.890
Sewers.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.650
Sewers?

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.610
It's pointless to pound on it.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.740
We need a better idea.

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.330
Exactly.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.540
Eggman!

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:56.290
I'm going to test the power of my new weapon: the Egg Spider!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.170
Wait!

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.380
Stop acting tough.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:13.270
Sonic!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.560
How dare you, Sonic!

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.070
You haven't defeated me yet!

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.370
Sonic!

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.210
Sonic!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.670
Screw Kick!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:45.680
Thanks.

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:47.510
Emerl?

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:50.520
I'm going to do my desperate attack!

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.270
I'll fight too!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:14.460
It's the Screw Kick.

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:25.930
What?

